  "chapter": 689,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 68 Chapter 689\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 4505, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the general business law and the mental hygiene\n        law, in relation to requiring warning labels on addictive social\n        media platforms\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  The bill would require the Commissioner of the Office of Mental Health\nto research, develop and design a warning label that social media  would\nthen be required to display to users.\n \n  I  support  the  goals of ensuring that young New Yorkers have healthy\nand safe experiences online. The bill, as drafted, is broad and  changes\nwere necessary to clarify the scope of the regulated platforms, the text\nof  the  warning  label  and  the design and display requirements of the\nlabel. I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to  enact  these\nchanges. On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2025
 },
